  "details": "I've had this bug occurring to me since the IK 2.0 came out, but I never thought much of since everyone tells me that my avatar looks fine. I'm reporting it since I think it's very weird that the issue seems to happen only locally.\n\nBasically, the eyes on my avatar break when using IK 2.0, giving my avatar a goofy look - But only for myself. This happens any time IK 2.0 is enabled, whenever I look at my avatar on mirrors, cameras, render textures, etc. I've been asking my friends if they see anything strange with my avatar when IK 2.0 is turned on, and everyone tells me the eyes look normal to them - and the pictures they send me look normal as well. \n\nI'm attaching 3 pictures. The (1) first one is how my avatar's eyes look when IK 2.0 is disabled. The (2) second picture is my avatar's eyes with the IK 2.0 enabled. The (3) third picture is one I got from a friend with IK 2.0 enabled (showing that it looked normal to him).",
